   "etymology": "From dialectal and archaic helq, though the further etymology is uncertain.\n* It may derive from Proto-Albanian *(w)alkja, from *h₂wolké-ye-ti, causative of Proto-Indo-European *h₂welk- (“to pull”) (compare Lithuanian velkù, Bulgarian влека́ (vleká, “to drag”), Greek αυλάκι (avláki, “furrow”)).\n* Perhaps from Proto-Indo-European *solk-éye-ti, from *selk-, whence also Latin sulcus.",
